# What a CI job installs by name in a workflow step and either nothing else
# declares (httpx) or CI holds at a version of its own (mypy). compile.py
# resolves these with the rest, so the step can install them under the same
# constraints file as everything else.

# The dashboard suite's test client (ci.yml, the autoresearch job). The page
# itself does not import it, so contrib/dashboard/requirements.txt has no pin.
httpx>=0.27

# The type-check job's mypy, at the one version its ``# type: ignore`` pins
# were written against (ci.yml says why it is exact). pyproject's dev extra
# asks for ``mypy>=2.0``; this line is what holds every file at this version,
# whatever compile.py is asked to upgrade. To move mypy: edit this line, run
# compile.py, and fix what the new version reports in the same pull request.
mypy==2.3.1
